.TH VIEWPORT 1 "2026-10-01" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
Viewport \- XR content creation environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Viewport
[\fB\-h\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]
[\fB\-i\fR \fIlang\fR]
[\fB\-nogui\fR]
[\fB\-mcp\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-silent\fR]
[\fB\-api\fR [\fIname\fR|\fB\-\-tui\fR]]
[\fB\-man\fR]
[\fB\-install\-man\fR]
Lightfielder is a hybrid computer-vision IDE/DCC toolset that unifies 
volumetric content creation from a single workspace.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Print version number and exit.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR \fIpython\fR|\fIlua\fR
Start an interactive REPL session in the given language. Supports multi-line
editing with arrow keys, command history (up/down arrows), inline syntax
highlighting, and the \fB==\fR shorthand for dumping Lua values. Enter
\fBlf.help()\fR to explore the scripting API from within the REPL.
.TP
\fB\-nogui\fR
Run headless with no windows or menu bar.
.TP
\fB\-mcp\fR
Run as an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server over stdio with no GUI.
Designed for AI coding assistants and render farm controllers.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-fullscreen\fR
Open the main window in native fullscreen.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-script\fR \fIpath\fR
Run a Lua or Python script file at the given path.
.TP
\fB\-silent\fR
Suppress all CLI output. Useful for render farm and automated workflows.
.TP
\fB\-api\fR [\fIname\fR]
List the entire scripting API with function descriptions, or show detailed help
for a specific function when \fIname\fR is provided.
.TP
\fB\-api\fR \fB\-\-tui\fR
Launch an interactive terminal help browser for the scripting API with
function and category listings, search, and detailed per-function help.
.PP
In GUI mode, palette windows can be toggled via function keys:
\fBF5\fR (History Stack), \fBF6\fR (Outliner), \fBF7\fR (Attributes),
\fBF8\fR (Script Console with REPL and Help Browser).
Additional viewport controls: \fBTab\fR opens the Create Dialog
(see CREATE DIALOG), \fBG\fR cycles grid modes, \fB`\fR (backtick)
toggles camera mode, and \fB/\fR toggles the HUD (see DISPLAY).
.TP
\fB\-man\fR
Open this man page using the bundled copy inside the app.
.TP
\fB\-install\-man\fR
Install the man page to \(ti/man/man1/Viewport.1 so future \fBman Viewport\fR
calls work system-wide.
.SH CREATE DIALOG
.PP
Pressing \fBTab\fR in the viewport opens a searchable Create Dialog
overlay for adding objects. Items are grouped by category:
.TP
\fBObjects\fR
Camera, Locator, Group, Reference, Note, Audio
.TP
\fBPrimitives\fR
Cube, Cone, Sphere, Cylinder, Pyramid, Torus
.TP
\fBLights\fR
Ambient, Area, Directional, Dome, Point, Spot, Sphere, Tube
.PP
Type to filter by name with autocomplete (gray suffix preview).
\fBUp\fR/\fBDown\fR arrows navigate, \fBEnter\fR confirms, \fBEscape\fR
dismisses.
.SH SCRIPTING API
Viewport embeds both Lua 5.4 and CPython 3.11 runtimes.
The full scripting API is exposed under the \fBlf\fR namespace.
Use \fB\-api\fR to list all functions, \fB\-api\fR \fB\-\-tui\fR for the
interactive browser, or \fBlf.help()\fR from a script or the REPL.
.PP
.SS Conventions
.PP
Lua functions return \fBtrue\fR on success or \fBnil, err\fR on failure.
Data-returning functions return a JSON string, or \fBnil, err\fR on failure.
.br
Python functions return \fBNone\fR on success and raise \fBRuntimeError\fR
on failure. Data-returning functions return native Python objects (list/dict).
.br
MCP uses JSON-RPC 2.0 over TCP (port 9876) or stdio (\fB\-mcp\fR).
The \fBmcp_server.py\fR wrapper (in Extras/) exposes all tools via the MCP
protocol with JSON Schema typed parameters.
.br
Primitive and light type names are lowercase in all three interfaces.
Display toggles accept boolean values.
