.SS Display Toggles
.PP
All display toggle functions accept a single boolean parameter:
\fBon\fR: \fBtrue\fR to show, \fBfalse\fR to hide.
.TP
\fBshow_grid\fR
Toggle grid visibility.
.TP
\fBshow_vertices\fR
Toggle vertex point display.
.TP
\fBshow_normals\fR
Toggle normal vector display.
.TP
\fBshow_edges\fR
Toggle wireframe edge overlay.
.TP
\fBshow_xray\fR
Toggle X-Ray transparency mode.
.TP
\fBshow_hud\fR
Toggle all HUD overlay elements.
.TP
\fBshow_fps\fR
Toggle the FPS counter in the HUD.
.TP
\fBshow_details\fR
Toggle detail/navigation info in the HUD.
.TP
\fBshow_distance\fR
Toggle distance measurement display.
.TP
\fBshow_render\fR
Toggle render style indicator display.
.TP
\fBshow_selected\fR
Toggle selection info display in the HUD.
.TP
\fBshow_camera_view\fR
Toggle camera view name display.
.TP
\fBshow_fov\fR
Toggle camera FOV display in the HUD.
.TP
\fBshow_polygons\fR
Toggle polygon count display.
.TP
\fBshow_camera_locators\fR
Toggle camera icon visibility in the viewport.
.TP
\fBshow_light_locators\fR
Toggle light icon visibility in the viewport.
.TP
\fBshow_locator_icons\fR
Toggle all locator icon visibility.
.TP
\fBshow_skybox\fR
Toggle skybox rendering.
.PP
Example usage:
.br
Lua:     \fBlf.show_grid(true)\fR
.br
Python:  \fBlf.show_grid(True)\fR
.br
MCP:     \fB{"method":"show_grid","params":[true],"id":1}\fR
