.SH INTERACTIVE REPL
.PP
When launched with \fB\-i lua\fR or \fB\-i python\fR, Viewport presents an
interactive REPL with the following features:
.TP
\fBUp / Down arrows\fR
Cycle through the command history. Previously entered lines can be recalled,
edited, and re-executed to fix syntax errors on the fly.
.TP
\fBLeft / Right arrows\fR
Move the text insertion cursor for inline editing. Home (Ctrl+A) and End
(Ctrl+E) jump to the line start and end.
.TP
\fBSyntax highlighting\fR
Lua and Python tokens are colorized in real time as you type: keywords
and literals (nil, true, false) in purple, strings in green, numbers in
gold, and function names in blue.
.TP
\fB\fB==\fR dump shortcut (Lua only)\fR
Prefix an expression with \fB==\fR to pretty-print it via the built-in
\fBdump()\fR function, e.g. \fB== lf\fR displays the full API table with
indentation and color.
.TP
\fBlf.help()\fR
Print detailed help for every scripting API function from within the REPL.
.TP
\fB$lua\fR and \fB$python\fR
Switch between the Lua and Python interpreters mid-session without
restarting. The prompt updates to reflect the current language.
.TP
\fBexit()\fR
End the REPL session.
.PP
The Lua REPL uses crash-safe evaluation (SIGSEGV/SIGBUS protection) so
that bugs in C extension code or the \fBdump()\fR pretty-printer produce
a recoverable error message instead of a hard crash.
.SH MCP SERVER
Viewport runs a JSON-RPC 2.0 server for MCP integration:
.TP
TCP mode (default):
Listens on port 9876 (configurable via \fBVIEWPORT_MCP_PORT\fR env var or
\fBMCPPort\fR UserDefaults). Used by the Python bridge in
\fBExtras/mcp_server.py\fR.
.TP
Stdio mode (\fB\-mcp\fR):
Communicates over stdin/stdout for direct integration with AI coding
assistants (Claude Desktop, opencode, etc.).
.PP
MCP clients discover tools via \fBtools/list\fR, which returns names,
descriptions, and JSON Schema input parameters. \fBtools/call\fR invokes a
tool by name with structured arguments. Available tools cover scene
management, object creation (audio, notes, groups, references), editing
(undo/redo, clipboard, duplicate, group/ungroup), transforms, viewport
controls, display toggles (grid, skybox, HUD, X-ray, etc.), window
panels, layouts, and app commands (about, quit, restart, share).
.PP
The \fBmcp_server.py\fR script (in Extras/) acts as a bridge: it connects
to the Viewport app's internal TCP JSON-RPC server and exposes every tool
via the MCP stdio protocol. If the \fBmcp\fR Python package is not
installed, it falls back to an interactive TCP test mode.
.SH DISPLAY
.PP
The viewport HUD overlays can be toggled together with \fB/\fR.
Individual elements (FPS, navigation details, distance, render style,
camera view, FOV, selection, polygon count) are toggleable from the
\fBView\fR menu and via scripting.
.PP
\fBG\fR cycles grid modes: Off \(-> Square Grid \(-> Disc Grid \(-> Off.
\fBSkybox\fR rendering is toggleable from the \fBView\fR menu or
\fBlf.show_skybox(Bool)\fR.
.SH WINDOW LAYOUTS
.PP
Window positions are persisted on quit, move, and resize. Pre-built layouts
(Compact, Default, Ultrawide, Laptop, etc.) appear under the \fBWindow\fR
menu; the first nine are bound to \fBCmd+1\fR through \fBCmd+9\fR.
Custom layouts can be saved via
\fBWindow > Save Window Layout\fR or \fBlf.save_layout(name)\fR
and loaded via \fBlf.load_layout(name)\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI*.jsonc\fR
Scene files in JSON with comments format.
.TP
\fI\(ti/Library/Application Support/com.Lightfielder.Viewport/\fR
Application support folder containing scripts, modules, and layouts.
.TP
\fI./Layouts/\fR
Saved window layout files (JSONC format).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Launch interactively in Lua:
Viewport \-i lua
.TP
Launch interactively in Python:
Viewport \-i python
.TP
Run a script and quit:
Viewport \-nogui \-s /path/to/script.py
.TP
Start MCP server for AI tools:
Viewport \-mcp
.TP
Explore the scripting API:
Viewport \-api
.TP
View help for a specific function:
Viewport \-api set_transform
.TP
Interactive API browser:
Viewport \-api \-\-tui
